## Media in this repo

- Geist and Geist Mono (`apps/web/public/fonts/*.woff2`): Copyright (c) 2023
  Vercel, in collaboration with basement.studio. Licensed under the SIL Open
  Font License 1.1; the license text is in `apps/web/public/fonts/OFL.txt`.
- Background music (`presets/music/*.mp3`): instrumental tracks made for
  ReelMakeEasy with ElevenLabs Music v2.5 (via fal) and picked by ear; each
  track's prompt is in `presets/LICENSES/music.md`.
- Kokoro and Qwen3-TTS preset-voice preview clips
  (`presets/voice-over/previews/preview-<voiceId>.mp3`): short lines spoken
  by those voices, generated on fal.
- Gemini preset-voice preview clips
  (`presets/voice-over/previews/preview-gemini-*.mp3`): generated on our own
  Gemini key.
- ElevenLabs preset-voice preview clips
  (`presets/voice-over/previews/preview-<ElevenLabs voice id>.mp3`):
  ElevenLabs's own sample clips for each voice, included so users can hear a
  voice before using it on their ElevenLabs or fal account.
- Interface images, Rive animations and example clips (`apps/web/public/static`,
  `libs/shared/ui/src/chat/assets`, `apps/web/src/app/favicon.ico`,
  `presets/style-preview-base.png`): Opus Pro, Inc.'s own artwork, licensed with
  the rest of this repo.

## In the preset pack (downloaded by setup, not in this repo; see presets/README.md)

- Fonts (`render/fonts.tar.gz`, `editor/storymode_fonts.tar.gz`):
  open-licensed fonts, unmodified: SIL Open Font License 1.1, and Apache-2.0
  for most Roboto weights. Each family's copyright and licence is listed in
  `presets/LICENSES/fonts.md`, with the licence texts beside it; the pack
  ships the same folder as `LICENSES/`.
- Camera samples (`camera-samples/*.mp4`, `camera-samples/*.jpg`): short
  clips from videos Opus Pro, Inc. made with AI video models, showing each
  camera style; Opus Pro, Inc.'s own media, licensed with the rest of this
  repo.

## Installed on your machine, not distributed with ReelMakeEasy

- Kokoro and Qwen3-TTS voice models: downloaded from Hugging Face by
  `pnpm reelmakeeasy setup`, distributed there under Apache-2.0. See
  `tools/local-tts/README.md`.
- Caption timing models, downloaded the same way: Whisper large-v3-turbo and
  small.en (MIT, in their MLX and CTranslate2 conversions), the Qwen3 forced
  aligner and wav2vec2 (Apache-2.0). faster-whisper and CTranslate2 are MIT.
- The local voice server's Python packages (`tools/local-tts/requirements-*.txt`)
  are installed from PyPI under their own licenses, among them GPL-3.0
  (phonemizer-fork, and eSpeak NG inside espeakng-loader) and LGPL
  (num2words).
- MongoDB: without a DATABASE_URL, `pnpm reelmakeeasy start` downloads MongoDB
  Community Server (SSPL-1.0) through mongodb-memory-server;
  `docker-compose.yml` uses the official mongo image.

